Table full name: bigquery-public-data.sunroof_solar.solar_potential_by_censustract
Column name: region_name Type: STRING Description: Census Tract
Column name: state_name Type: STRING Description: Name of the state containing that region
Column name: lat_max Type: FLOAT64 Description: maximum latitude for that region
Column name: lat_min Type: FLOAT64 Description: minimum latitude for that region
Column name: lng_max Type: FLOAT64 Description: maximum longitude for that region
Column name: lng_min Type: FLOAT64 Description: minimum longitude for that region
Column name: lat_avg Type: FLOAT64 Description: average latitude for that region
Column name: lng_avg Type: FLOAT64 Description: average longitude for that region
Column name: yearly_sunlight_kwh_kw_threshold_avg Type: FLOAT64 Description: 75% of the optimimum sunlight in the county containing that zip code
Column name: count_qualified Type: INT64 Description: # of buildings in Google Maps that are suitable for solar
Column name: percent_covered Type: FLOAT64 Description: % of buildings in Google Maps covered by Project Sunroof
Column name: percent_qualified Type: FLOAT64 Description: % of buildings covered by Project Sunroof that are suitable for solar
Column name: number_of_panels_n Type: INT64 Description: # of solar panels potential for north-facing roof space in that region, assuming 1.650m x 0.992m panels
Column name: number_of_panels_s Type: INT64 Description: # of solar panels potential for south-facing roof space in that region, assuming 1.650m x 0.992m panels
Column name: number_of_panels_e Type: INT64 Description: # of solar panels potential for east-facing roof space in that region, assuming 1.650m x 0.992m panels
Column name: number_of_panels_w Type: INT64 Description: # of solar panels potential for west-facing roof space in that region, assuming 1.650m x 0.992m panels
Column name: number_of_panels_f Type: INT64 Description: # of solar panels potential for flat roof space in that region, assuming 1.650m x 0.992m panels
Column name: number_of_panels_median Type: INT64 Description: # of panels that fit on the median roof
Column name: number_of_panels_total Type: INT64 Description: # of solar panels potential for all roof space in that region, assuming 1.650m 0.992m panels
Column name: kw_median Type: FLOAT64 Description: kW of solar potential for the median building in that region (assuming 250 watts per panel)
Column name: kw_total Type: FLOAT64 Description: # of kW of solar potential for all roof types in that region (assuming 250 watts per panel)
Column name: yearly_sunlight_kwh_n Type: FLOAT64 Description: total solar energy generation potential for north-facing roof space in that region
Column name: yearly_sunlight_kwh_s Type: FLOAT64 Description: total solar energy generation potential for south-facing roof space in that region
Column name: yearly_sunlight_kwh_e Type: FLOAT64 Description: total solar energy generation potential for east-facing roof space in that region
Column name: yearly_sunlight_kwh_w Type: FLOAT64 Description: total solar energy generation potential for west-facing roof space in that region
Column name: yearly_sunlight_kwh_f Type: FLOAT64 Description: total solar energy generation potential for flat roof space in that region
Column name: yearly_sunlight_kwh_median Type: FLOAT64 Description: kWh/kw/yr for the median roof, in DC (not AC) terms
Column name: yearly_sunlight_kwh_total Type: FLOAT64 Description: total solar energy generation potential for all roof space in that region
Column name: install_size_kw_buckets Type: STRING Description: # of buildings with potential for various installation size buckets. Format is a JSON array, where each element is a tuple containing (1) lower bound of bucket, in kW, and (2) number of buildings in that bucket.
Column name: carbon_offset_metric_tons Type: FLOAT64 Description: The potential carbon dioxide abatement of the solar capacity that meets the technical potential criteria. The calculation uses eGRID subregion CO2 equivalent non-baseload output emission rates. https://www.epa.gov/sites/production/files/2015-10/documents/egrid2012_summarytables_0.pdf
Column name: existing_installs_count Type: INT64 Description: # of buildings estimated to have a solar installation, at time of data collection
Column name: center_point Type: GEOGRAPHY
